    <!-- prettier-ignore -->
    <p class="max-w-4xl text-lg sm:text-2xl font-medium leading-snug text-ink/90">
      I built OmniBuf because I wanted a binary format that fixes the parts of <a href="https://protobuf.dev/programming-guides/encoding/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="doc-link">Protobuf</a> that have aged poorly since 2001 (like <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/LEB128" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="doc-link">LEB128 varints</a> and two-pass encoding), while also working as a fast, compact replacement for <strong>JSON</strong> on normal structs.
    </p>

    <div class="grid lg:grid-cols-12 gap-5 items-stretch">
